fs/ntfs3: free the mft_inode when mi_format_new() fails in do_action()

When log replay initialises a file record segment that cannot be read,
do_action() allocates a struct mft_inode and formats it with
mi_format_new(). If that fails, do_action() returns the error without
releasing mi (and mi->mrec when mi_init() succeeded). Release it with
mi_put(), as the out label does on the normal path.
---
--- a/fs/ntfs3/fslog.c	2026-10-20 14:44:39.611152580 +0000
+++ b/fs/ntfs3/fslog.c	2026-10-20 14:44:39.629492130 +0000
@@ -3168,6 +3168,11 @@
 				if (!mi)
 					return -ENOMEM;
 				err = mi_format_new(mi, sbi, rno, 0, false);
+				if (err) {
+					/* mi is not attached anywhere yet. */
+					mi_put(mi);
+					return err;
+				}
 			}
 			if (err)
 				return err;
